Follow each of the four roads in the drawing:
- one road starts at Carol's house and ends on the right below Ben;
- one road starts at Ben's house and ends at the top left;
- one road starts at David's house and ends at the bottom;
- one road starts at Amy's house and ends on the right.

Two straight roads can cross at most once. In the drawing, Carol's road crosses Ben's road **twice** (the eye shape on the left) and also crosses Amy's road twice (the eye shape on the right). In each of these pairs one road must be the curved one. The only road in both pairs is Carol's, so Carol lives on Qurwik Road.

**Answer: (C) Carol**
